MathCAT: with a decimal comma, a list separator after a decimal number starts no new number

With the DecimalSeparator preference set to "," (MateX's default, so that
`1,5` reads as one number), `{1,5, 2}` came out as "the set 1,5,2":
`merge_number_blocks` skips the `mn` "1,5" as already parsed, but then
takes the following `mo` "," for the decimal separator of a new number
and merges it with "2" into ",2". A comma (or other decimal separator)
right after an `mn` that already contains a decimal separator now starts
no number; it stays the list separator.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Worth
proposing upstream to daisy/MathCAT.

--- a/src/canonicalize.rs
+++ b/src/canonicalize.rs
@@ -2113,7 +2113,11 @@
 					}
 				} else if child_name != "mo" ||
 						  (do_not_merge_comma && as_text(child) == ",") ||
-						  !context.patterns.decimal_separator.is_match(as_str!(as_text(child))) {
+						  !context.patterns.decimal_separator.is_match(as_str!(as_text(child))) ||
+						  // MateX: a separator right after a number that already has its decimal separator
+						  //   ("1,5" "," "2" with a decimal comma) separates numbers; it does not start ",2"
+						  (i > 0 && name(as_element(children[i-1])) == "mn" &&
+						   context.patterns.decimal_separator.is_match(as_str!(as_text(as_element(children[i-1]))))) {
 					i += 1;
 					continue;
 				}
